027)?\",\n          \"outcome\": \"NVIDIA's reported total revenue for fiscal 2027, versus the roughly $412 billion analysts' consensus cited in the item and the trajectory implied by fiscal Q2 revenue of $96.2 billion and fiscal Q3 guidance of $108 billion.\",\n          \"period\": \"Fiscal 2027 (year ending late January 2027); settled at the release of NVIDIA's fiscal 2027 fourth-quarter results and Form 10-K, expected around February 2027 — the release of that fiscal year's results, per section 3.\",\n          \"settled_by\": \"NVIDIA's fiscal 2027 fourth-quarter and full-year results release and its fiscal 2027 Form 10-K, which state total annual revenue.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"new-2\",\n          \"question\": \"What total revenue will NVIDIA report for fiscal 2028 (the year ending January 2028), given management's guidance of roughly 70% growth on a supply-constrained outlook?\",\n          \"outcome\": \"NVIDIA's reported total revenue for fiscal 2028 versus the roughly 70% growth management guided, and whether the constraint proves to be manufacturing capacity rather than demand.\",\n          \"period\": \"Fiscal 2028 (year ending late January 2028); settled at the release of NVIDIA's fiscal 2028 fourth-quarter results and Form 10-K, expected around February 2028 — the release of that fiscal year's results, per section 3.\",\n          \"settled_by\": \"NVIDIA's fiscal 2028 fourth-quarter and full-year results release and its fiscal 2028 Form 10-K, which state total annual revenue.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"new-3\",\n          \"question\": \"What gross margin will NVIDIA report for fiscal 2028 (the year ending January 2028), after management guided it to bottom at 71%–72% in fiscal Q4 2027 and settle at 72%–73% in fiscal 2028?\",\n          \"outcome\": \"NVIDIA's reported fiscal 2028 gross margin versus the 72%–73% management guidance and the fiscal Q2 2027 level of 75%, and whether the contemplated price increases materialise.\",\n          \"period\": \"Fiscal 2028 (year ending late January 2028); settled at the release of NVIDIA's fiscal 2028 fourth-quarter results and Form 10-K, expected around February 2028 — the release of that fiscal year's results, per section 3.\",\n          \"settled_by\": \"NVIDIA's fiscal 2028 fourth-quarter and full-year results release and its fiscal 2028 Form 10-K, which report the annual gross margin.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"kept_statements\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-1\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA reported fiscal 2027 second-quarter revenue (quarter ended July 26, 2026) of $96.2 billion, up 106% year over year and faster than the fiscal first quarter's 85% year-over-year growth, with data center contributing $89 billion of the total and net income of $59.7 billion, up 126% year over year.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Nvidia's latest results make the growth requirement seem nearly routine. Revenue in the fiscal 2027 second quarter (the period ended July 26, 2026) came to $96.2 billion, up 106% over a year earlier. This pace was even faster than the fiscal first quarter's 85% year-over-year growth. The data center business made up $89 billion of the total. And net income , at $59.7 billion, rose 126% year over year.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-1\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"NVIDIA's own quarterly revenue and data center revenue are direct components of the fiscal 2027 total-revenue question; the reported figures are actuals, not guidance. The net income figure is listed for completeness but is not the thesis quantity.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-2\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA guided fiscal 2027 third-quarter revenue to $108 billion, around 12% above its fiscal second-quarter revenue.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Guidance for the fiscal third quarter is $108 billion in revenue , around 12% above fiscal Q2.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-1\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"Company guidance for the next quarter is a direct input to the fiscal 2027 annual revenue total; it is guidance, not a reported result.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-3\",\n          \"summary\": \"On NVIDIA's late-August fiscal 2027 second-quarter earnings call, CFO Colette Kress said the company expects revenue to rise roughly 70% in fiscal 2028, the year ending January 2028, and called it \\\"a supply-constrained outlook\\\", with the limit being manufacturing capacity rather than customer demand.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"And on the company's late-August earnings call, CFO Colette Kress said Nvidia expects revenue to rise roughly 70% in fiscal 2028, the year ending in January 2028. She called it \\\"a supply-constrained outlook.\\\" Put another way, the limit is manufacturing capacity, not customer demand.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-2\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"Management's own fiscal 2028 revenue growth guidance and its statement that supply, not demand, is the constraint directly set the fiscal 2028 revenue question; this is a forecast, not a reported outcome.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-4\",\n          \"summary\": \"On the same earnings call, NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said gross margins should bottom between 71% and 72% in the fiscal fourth quarter and then settle at 72% to 73% in fiscal 2028 as price hikes kick in, a small drop from the 75% gross margin reported in the fiscal second quarter.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Margins might not change the picture much, either. On the call, Kress said gross margins should bottom between 71% and 72% in the fiscal fourth quarter and then settle at 72% to 73% in fiscal 2028 as price hikes kick in. That'd be a drop from the fiscal second quarter's 75%, though a small one.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-3\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"Management's gross margin guidance for the fiscal fourth quarter (71%–72%) and fiscal 2028 (72%–73%), set against the 75% fiscal Q2 level and tied to expected price hikes, directly bears on the fiscal 2028 gross-margin question; these are forecasts, not reported results.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-5\",\n          \"summary\": \"Analysts' consensus had NVIDIA's fiscal 2027 revenue coming in around $412 billion.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Analysts' consensus already has fiscal 2027 revenue coming in around $412 billion.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-1\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"The consensus estimate for fiscal 2027 total revenue is a benchmark for the fiscal 2027 revenue question; it is an estimate, not a reported result.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"answer\": \"A07\",\n      \"article\": 9,\n      \"new_questions\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"N1\",\n          \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA report fiscal 2028 total revenue growth of about 70% year over year, as management has guided in its first full-year outlook?\",\n          \"outcome\": \"NVIDIA's reported fiscal 2028 total revenue and year-over-year growth versus the ~70% management guidance.\",\n          \"period\": \"Fiscal 2028 (fiscal year ending late January 2028); settled by NVIDIA's Q4 FY2028 results and FY2028 Form 10-K, expected around February 2028 — the release of that fiscal year's results, per section 3 ([reason]).\",\n          \"settled_by\": \"NVIDIA's quarterly results and fiscal 2028 Form 10-K, which report total revenue and year-over-year growth.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"N2\",\n          \"question\": \"What gross margin will NVIDIA report for fiscal 2028, against its guidance of a 72%–73% range as memory prices rise?\",\n          \"outcome\": \"NVIDIA's reported fiscal 2028 gross margin versus the 72%–73% guided range, given higher-than-expected memory prices and price increases already executed.\",\n          \"period\": \"Fiscal 2028 (fiscal year ending late January 2028); settled by NVIDIA's Q4 FY2028 results and FY2028 Form 10-K, expected around February 2028 — the release of that fiscal year's results, per section 3 ([reason]).\",\n          \"settled_by\": \"NVIDIA's fiscal 2028 quarterly results and Form 10-K gross margin disclosure.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"kept_statements\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e1\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA management expects Vera Rubin, its newest platform, to be the fastest product ramp in the company's history and puts the revenue opportunity at about $40 billion per gigawatt of capacity with Vera Rubin, against $25 billion with Blackwell.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"NVIDIA expects Vera Rubin, its newest platform, to be the fastest product ramp in the company’s history. Management puts NVIDIA’s revenue opportunity at about $40 billion per gigawatt of capacity with Vera Rubin, against $25 billion with Blackwell.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"clean-4\",\n              \"new\": false,\n              \"why\": \"Management's per-gigawatt revenue framing for Vera Rubin (about $40bn/GW vs $25bn with Blackwell) and its 'fastest ramp in history' expectation quantify the economics of the platform whose ramp to volume shipments the thesis tracks; they do not establish shipment volumes or timing.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \