-than-expected memory prices, partly offset by executed price increases) — the quantity the thesis tracks.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e6\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA has invested nearly $50 billion in frontier AI labs; management acknowledges some will call this circular financing and says the compute can be redeployed to other customers.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"NVIDIA has invested nearly $50 billion in frontier AI labs. Management concedes some will call this circular financing and says the compute can be redeployed to other customers.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"clean-1\",\n              \"new\": false,\n              \"why\": \"Supplies the equity-investment side of the comparison the thesis tracks — nearly $50bn invested in frontier AI labs — against the guarantees and credit support NVIDIA may disclose; it does not itself quantify any guarantees or backstops.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e7\",\n          \"summary\": \"The 33 analyst estimates of NVIDIA's fiscal 2028 earnings range from $12.62 to $17.49 a share, a wide band for the year on which the forward multiple is priced.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Analysts also disagree on what that growth earns. The 33 estimates of fiscal 2028 earnings run from $12.62 to $17.49 a share, a wide band for the year the forward multiple is priced on.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e8\",\n          \"summary\": \"Trefis wrote that consensus expects NVIDIA's earnings and revenue to grow at a similar pace between fiscal 2027 and fiscal 2028, implying analysts assume profit margins hold roughly steady.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Consensus has earnings and revenue growing at a similar pace between fiscal 2027 and fiscal 2028, so analysts assume profit margins 