nues increased about 20% sequentially and nearly tripled year over year. During the last earnings call, management noted that purpose-built silicon revenues are approaching an estimated $2 billion run rate, and the company is targeting $4 billion in the near future.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"answer\": \"A11\",\n      \"article\": 10,\n      \"new_questions\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"new-nvda-fy2027-revenue\",\n          \"question\": \"What total revenue will NVIDIA report for fiscal 2027, the year ending late January 2027?\",\n          \"outcome\": \"NVIDIA's reported total revenue for fiscal 2027, compared with the fiscal Q2 actual of $96.2 billion, fiscal Q3 guidance of $108 billion and analysts' consensus of about $412 billion.\",\n          \"period\": \"NVIDIA fiscal 2027 annual results (Form 10-K expected around February 2027) — the release of that fiscal year's results, per [reason].\",\n          \"settled_by\": \"NVIDIA's fiscal 2027 fourth-quarter and full-year results and Form 10-K.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"new-nvda-fy2028-revenue\",\n          \"question\": \"What total revenue will NVIDIA report for fiscal 2028, the year ending January 2028?\",\n          \"outcome\": \"NVIDIA's reported total revenue for fiscal 2028, compared with the CFO's expectation of roughly 70% growth and the article's calculation of about $700 billion.\",\n          \"period\": \"NVIDIA fiscal 2028 annual results (Form 10-K expected around February 2028) — the release of that fiscal year's results, per [reason].\",\n          \"settled_by\": \"NVIDIA's fiscal 2028 fourth-quarter and full-year results and Form 10-K.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"new-nvda-fy2028-gross-margin\",\n          \"question\": \"What gross margin will NVIDIA report for fiscal 2028, the year ending January 2028?\",\n          \"outcome\": \"NVIDIA's reported fiscal 2028 gross margin, compared with the CFO's expectation that it settles at 72% to 73%, after bottoming at 71% to 72% in fiscal Q4 2027 and versus 75% in fiscal Q2 2027.\",\n          \"period\": \"NVIDIA fiscal 2028 annual results (Form 10-K expected around February 2028) — the release of that fiscal year's results, per [reason].\",\n          \"settled_by\": \"NVIDIA's fiscal 2028 fourth-quarter and full-year results and Form 10-K.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"kept_statements\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e1\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA reported fiscal 2027 second-quarter revenue of $96.2 billion, up 106% from a year earlier and faster than the fiscal first quarter's 85% year-over-year growth, with the data center business contributing $89 billion; net income was $59.7 billion, up 126% year over year, for the quarter ended July 26, 2026.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Revenue in the fiscal 2027 second quarter (the period ended July 26, 2026) came to $96.2 billion, up 106% over a year earlier. This pace was even faster than the fiscal first quarter's 85% year-over-year growth. The data center business made up $89 billion of the total. And net income , at $59.7 billion, rose 126% year over year.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-nvda-fy2027-revenue\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"Reported fiscal Q2 2027 revenue, data center revenue and net income are actual current-year results directly informing the fiscal 2027 annual revenue outcome.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-nvda-fy2028-revenue\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"The Q2 2027 revenue level and 106% year-over-year growth provide a run-rate/base that informs the fiscal 2028 revenue trajectory, though they are prior-period figures.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e2\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA guided fiscal 2027 third-quarter revenue to $108 billion, which the article says is around 12% above fiscal Q2.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Guidance for the fiscal third quarter is $108 billion in revenue , around 12% above fiscal Q2.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-nvda-fy2027-revenue\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"Fiscal Q3 2027 revenue guidance is a direct company forecast for the current fiscal year's annual revenue.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-nvda-fy2028-revenue\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"Fiscal Q3 2027 guidance provides a near-term run-rate/base for the fiscal 2028 revenue question, though it is not an FY2028 figure.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e3\",\n          \"summary\": \"On the late-August 2026 earnings call, NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said NVIDIA expects revenue to rise roughly 70% in fiscal 2028, the year ending January 2028, and called it \\\"a supply-constrained outlook\\\"; the article paraphrased this as manufacturing capacity, not customer demand, being the limit.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"And on the company's late-August earnings call, CFO Colette Kress said Nvidia expects revenue to rise roughly 70% in fiscal 2028, the year ending in January 2028. She called it \\\"a supply-constrained outlook.\\\" Put another way, the limit is manufacturing capacity, not customer demand.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-nvda-fy2028-revenue\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"The CFO's roughly 70% fiscal 2028 revenue growth guidance and supply-constrained outlook directly inform the fiscal 2028 annual revenue question, though the item gives a growth rate rather than an absolute level.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"question\": \"clean-2\",\n              \"new\": false,\n              \"why\": \"Management says the outlook is supply-constrained and that manufacturing capacity, not customer demand, is the limit, which bears on the need for purchase/supply commitments; no commitment amount or obligation is stated.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e4\",\n          \"summary\": \"In this article, analysts' consensus has NVIDIA's fiscal 2027 revenue at around $412 billion, and the article elsewhere refers to \\\"this fiscal year's expected 90% revenue growth\\\"; applying the CFO's roughly 70% growth rate implies fiscal 2028 revenue of somewhere around $700 billion.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Analysts' consensus already has fiscal 2027 revenue coming in around $412 billion. Grow that by roughly 70%, and fiscal 2028 lands somewhere around $700 billion.\",\n            \"Next to this fiscal year's expected 90% revenue growth and next year's forecast 70%, that would arguably be a low bar.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-nvda-fy2027-revenue\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"Analysts' consensus fiscal 2027 revenue of about $412 billion and the article's reference to expected 90% fiscal 2027 revenue growth are direct estimates for the fiscal 2027 annual revenue thesis.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-nvda-fy2028-revenue\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"The article's calculation of about $700 billion fiscal 2028 revenue, using the CFO's roughly 70% growth on the consensus base, directly informs the fiscal 2028 annual revenue thesis.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e5\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said on the call that gross margins should bottom at 71% to 72% in fiscal Q4 2027 and then settle at 72% to 73% in fiscal 2028 as price hikes kick in; the article notes this compares with fiscal Q2 2027 gross margin of 75%.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"On the call, Kress said gross margins should bottom between 71% and 72% in the fiscal fourth quarter and then settle at 72% to 73% in fiscal 2028 as price hikes kick in. That'd be a drop from the fiscal second quarter's 75%, though a small one.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-nvda-fy2028-gross-margin\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"The CFO's guidance for gross margin to settle at 72% to 73% in fiscal 2028, after bottoming at 71% to 72% in fiscal Q4 2027 and versus 75% in fiscal Q2 2027, directly informs the fiscal 2028 annual gross margin thesis.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"answer\": \"A12\",\n      \"article\": 5,\n      \"new_questions\": [],\n      \"kept_statements\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e1\",\n          \"summary\": \"Nvidia's revenue and net income are each expected to grow by roughly 90% or more in its current fiscal year, even as the stock trades near its lowest valuation in more than a decade, according to expectations reported by qz.com citing Bloomberg. The actor is the consensus expectation (unnamed forecasters) as reported by the outlet; it is a forecast for the current fiscal year, not a reported result.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Nvidia $NVDA stock is trading near its lowest valuation in more than a decade, according to Bloomberg , even as the chipmaker's revenue and net income are each expected to grow by roughly 90% or more in its current fiscal year.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e2\",\n          \"summary\": \"Nvidia's gross margin came in at 75% in its most recent quarter, and analyst estimates compiled by Bloomberg show it sliding under 72% by the fourth quarter, with a recovery expected thereafter; rising costs for key components such as memory chips are cited as a central factor. Reported actual versus forecast are distinct: 75% is a reported result, the sub-72% figure is an estimate.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Nvidia 's gross margin came in at 75% last quarter but analyst estimates compiled by Bloomberg show it sliding under 72% by the fourth quarter, with a recovery expected thereafter.\",\n            \"Rising costs for key components such as memory chips are a central factor.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e3\",\n          \"summary\": \"Nvidia's revenue more than doubled year over year in its most recent quarter, and the company projected 70% revenue growth in fiscal 2028, well above the 45% analysts had expected at the time, according to qz.com. The 70% figure is company guidance; the 45% figure was the prior consensus.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Nvidia stock climbed roughly 7% after its second-quarter earnings , when revenue more than doubled and the company projected 70% revenue growth in fiscal 2028 — well above the 45% analysts had expected at the time.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e4\",\n          \"summary\": \"David Russell, global head of market strategy at TradeStation, said the growing threat of customers building their own silicon — noting that Meta and Alphabet are among the major Nvidia buyers that have moved to design AI chips internally — will gradually erode Nvidia's pricing power and market share. This is his opinion; the item gives no date, volume or contract detail for the in-house chip efforts.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Competition is another concern. David Russell, global head of market strategy at TradeStation, pointed to the growing threat of customers building their own silicon, noting that Meta $META Platforms and Alphabet $GOOGL are among the major Nvidia buyers that have moved to design AI chips internally — a shift he believes will gradually erode Nvidia 's pricing power and market share.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"answer\": \"A13\",\n      \"article\": 2,\n      \"new_questions\": [],\n      \"kept_statements\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-1\",\n          \"summary\": \"The Zacks Consensus Estimate projects NVIDIA will post earnings of $2.47 per share in the current quarter, a change of +90% from the year-ago quarter; the consensus figure itself moved +5.8% over the last 30 days.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"For the current quarter, Nvidia is expected to post earnings of $2.47 per share, indicating a change of +90% from the year-ago quarter. The Zacks Consensus Estimate has changed +5.8% over the last 30 days.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-2\",\n          \"summary\": \"The Zacks Consensus Estimate projects NVIDIA earnings of $9.25 per share for the current fiscal year, a change of +93.9% from the prior year, with the estimate up +5.1% over the last 30 days.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"For the current fiscal year, the consensus earnings estimate of $9.25 points to a change of +93.9% from the prior year. Over the last 30 days, this estimate has changed +5.1%.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-3\",\n          \"summary\": \"The Zacks Consensus Estimate projects NVIDIA earnings of $15.33 per share for the next fiscal year, a change of +65.8% from what NVIDIA is expected to report a year earlier, and the estimate rose +21.8% over the past month.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"For the next fiscal year, the consensus earnings estimate of $15.33 indicates a change of +65.8% from what Nvidia is expected to report a year ago. Over the past month, the estimate has changed +21.8%.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-4\",\n          \"summary\": \"The consensus sales estimate for NVIDIA's current quarter is $109.02 billion, a year-over-year change of +91.2%.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"For Nvidia, the consensus sales estimate for the current quarter of $109.02 billion indicates a year-over-year change of +91.2%.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-5\",\n          \"summary\": \"Consensus sales estimates for NVIDIA are $406.05 billion for the current fiscal year and $671.95 billion for the next fiscal year, indicating changes of +88% and +65.5% respectively.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"For the current and next fiscal years, $406.05 billion and $671.95 billion estimates indicate +88% and +65.5% changes, respectively.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"answer\": \"A14\",\n      \"article\": 6,\n      \"new_questions\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"answer\": \"A15\",\n      \"article\": 5,\n      \"new_questions\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"nt-1\",\n          \"question\": \"How much will NVIDIA's total revenue grow in fiscal 2027, against the roughly 90%-or-more growth consensus reported in this item?\",\n          \"outcome\": \"NVIDIA's fiscal 2027 total revenue growth versus fiscal 2026, against the roughly 90%-or-more consensus expectation.\",\n          \"period\": \"Fiscal 2027 results release (Form 10-K expected around February 2027) — the current fiscal year's annual results.\",\n          \"settled_by\": \"NVIDIA's fiscal 2027 Form 10-K and annual results release (expected around February 2027).\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"nt-2\",\n          \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA's total revenue grow about 70% in fiscal 2028, as the company projected?\",\n          \"outcome\": \"NVIDIA's fiscal 2028 total revenue growth versus fiscal 2027, against the company's 70% projection.\",\n          \"period\": \"Fiscal 2028 results release (Form 10-K expected around February 2028) — the next fiscal year's annual results.\",\n          \"settled_by\": \"NVIDIA's fiscal 2028 Form 10-K and annual results release (expected around February 2028).\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"nt-3\",\n          \"question\": \"What will NVIDIA's gross margin be for fiscal 2027, against the 75% reported last quarter and analyst estimates of sub-72% by the fourth quarter?\",\n          \"outcome\": \"NVIDIA's fiscal 2027 annual gross margin and its quarterly trajectory, against the 75% reported last quarter and the sub-72% fourth-quarter estimate.\",\n          \"period\": \"Fiscal 2027 annual report (Form 10-K expected around February 2027) — the current fiscal year's annual gross margin and fourth-quarter result.\",\n          \"settled_by\": \"NVIDIA's fiscal 2027 Form 10-K and annual results release (expected around February 2027), including quarterly gross margin.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"kept_statements\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-1\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA projected 70% revenue growth for fiscal 2028, well above the 45% analysts had expected at the time, according to Quartz's report on the company's second-quarter earnings.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Nvidia stock climbed roughly 7% after its second-quarter earnings , when revenue more than doubled and the company projected 70% revenue growth in fiscal 2028 — well above the 45% analysts had expected at the time.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"nt-2\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"The company's own 70% fiscal 2028 revenue growth projection is the outcome this thesis tracks.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-2\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA's revenue and net income are each expected to grow by roughly 90% or more in its current fiscal year (fiscal 2027), according to expectations reported by Quartz.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"even as the chipmaker's revenue and net income are each expected to grow by roughly 90% or more in its current fiscal year.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"nt-1\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"The consensus expectation for current-fiscal-year revenue growth is the outcome this thesis tracks.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-3\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA's gross margin came in at 75% in its most recently reported quarter ('last quarter'), according to Quartz.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Nvidia 's gross margin came in at 75% last quarter\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"nt-3\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"The reported 75% gross margin is the starting point for the fiscal 2027 gross-margin thesis.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-4\",\n          \"summary\": \"Analyst estimates compiled by Bloomberg show NVIDIA's gross margin sliding under 72% by the fourth quarter, with a recovery expected thereafter; rising costs for key components such as memory chips are a central factor, according to Quartz.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"but analyst estimates compiled by Bloomberg show it sliding under 72% by the fourth quarter, with a recovery expected thereafter.\",\n            \"Rising costs for key components such as memory chips are a central factor.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"nt-3\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"The analyst estimate of fourth-quarter gross-margin compression and the memory-cost driver inform the fiscal 2027 gross-margin thesis.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-5\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA's revenue more than doubled in its second quarter, according to Quartz's report on the earnings that preceded the fiscal 2028 growth projection.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Nvidia stock climbed roughly 7% after its second-quarter earnings , when revenue more than doubled and the company projected 70% revenue growth in fiscal 2028 — well above the 45% analysts had expected at the time.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"nt-1\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"Second-quarter revenue more than doubling is an actual data point supporting the current-fiscal-year revenue-growth thesis.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"answer\": \"A16\",\n      \"article\": 1,\n      \"new_questions\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"answer\": \"A17\",\n      \"article\": 3,\n      \"new_questions\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"answer\": \"A18\",\n      \"article\": 2,\n      \"new_questions\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"rev_fy27\",\n          \"question\": \"What total revenue will NVIDIA report for its current fiscal year (the fiscal year ending late January 2027)?\",\n          \"outcome\": \"NVIDIA's reported total revenue for the current fiscal year, to be compared with the $406.05 billion consensus sales estimate cited in the 22 September 2026 Zacks article.\",\n          \"period\": \"Current fiscal year (FY2027, ending late January 2027) — set from the item's 'current fiscal year' consensus estimate; settled by NVIDIA's release of that fiscal year's results and Form 10-K, expected around February 2027.\",\n          \"settled_by\": \"NVIDIA's reported quarterly and annual results and its Form 10-K for the fiscal year ending late January 2027.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"rev_fy28\",\n          \"question\": \"What total revenue will NVIDIA report for its next fiscal year (the fiscal year ending late January 2028)?\",\n          \"outcome\": \"NVIDIA's reported total revenue for the next fiscal year, to be compared with the $671.95 billion consensus sales estimate cited in the 22 September 2026 Zacks article.\",\n          \"period\": \"Next fiscal year (FY2028, ending late January 2028) — set from the item's 'next fiscal year' consensus estimate; settled by the release of that fiscal year's results and Form 10-K, expected around February 2028.\",\n          \"settled_by\": \"NVIDIA's reported results and Form 10-K for the fiscal year ending late January 2028.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"kept_statements\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e1\",\n          \"summary\": \"Zacks reported that, as of its 22 September 2026 article, the consensus expects NVIDIA to post earnings of $2.47 per share in the current quarter, a +90% change from the year-ago quarter, and that the Zacks Consensus Estimate for that quarter had changed +5.8% over the prior 30 days.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"For the current quarter, Nvidia is expected to post earnings of $2.47 per share, indicating a change of +90% from the year-ago quarter. The Zacks Consensus Estimate has changed +5.8% over the last 30 days.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e2\",\n          \"summary\": \"Zacks reported that the consensus earnings estimate for NVIDIA's current fiscal year was $9.25 per share, pointing to a +93.9% change from the prior year, and that the estimate had changed +5.1% over the prior 30 days.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"For the current fiscal year, the consensus earnings estimate of $9.25 points to a change of +93.9% from the prior year. Over the last 30 days, this estimate has changed +5.1%.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e3\",\n          \"summary\": \"Zacks reported that the consensus earnings estimate for NVIDIA's next fiscal year was $15.33 per share, indicating a +65.8% change from what NVIDIA is expected to report a year earlier, and that the estimate had changed +21.8% over the past month.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"For the next fiscal year, the consensus earnings estimate of $15.33 indicates a change of +65.8% from what Nvidia is expected to report a year ago. Over the past month, the estimate has changed +21.8%.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e4\",\n          \"summary\": \"Zacks reported consensus sales estimates for NVIDIA of $109.02 billion for the current quarter (+91.2% year over year) and, for the current and next fiscal years, $406.05 billion (+88%) and $671.95 billion (+65.5%), respectively, as of its 22 September 2026 article.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"For Nvidia, the consensus sales estimate for the current quarter of $109.02 billion indicates a year-over-year change of +91.2%. For the current and next fiscal years, $406.05 billion and $671.95 billion estimates indicate +88% and +65.5% changes, respectively.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"rev_fy27\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"The $406.05 billion consensus sales estimate for the current fiscal year is a direct benchmark for NVIDIA's FY2027 reported total revenue; the $109.02 billion current-quarter estimate is a component of that annual path. Both are estimates, not guidance or reported results.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"question\": \"rev_fy28\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"The $671.95 billion consensus sales estimate for the next fiscal year is a direct benchmark for NVIDIA's FY2028 reported total revenue. It is a consensus estimate, not company guidance or an actual result.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"answer\": \"A19\",\n      \"article\": 3,\n      \"new_questions\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"answer\": \"A20\",\n      \"article\": 9,\n      \"new_questions\": [],\n      \"kept_statements\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e1\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA management said it expects Vera Rubin, its newest AI platform, to be the fastest product ramp in the company's history, putting NVIDIA's revenue opportunity at about $40 billion per gigawatt of capacity with Vera Rubin versus $25 billion with Blackwell.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"NVIDIA expects Vera Rubin, its newest platform, to be the fastest product ramp in the company’s history. Management puts NVIDIA’s revenue opportunity at about $40 billion per gigawatt of capacity with Vera Rubin, against $25 billion with Blackwell.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"clean-4\",\n              \"new\": false,\n              \"why\": \"Management's expected Vera Rubin ramp and per-gigawatt revenue opportunity bear on whether the platform can become a volume revenue product; this is a forward-looking company claim, not confirmation of volume shipments.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e2\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA's Vera Rubin production shipments began in August 2026, with purchase orders already received from every major hyperscaler, AI cloud provider and system OEM, according to the article.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Production shipments began in August, with purchase orders already in from every major hyperscaler, AI cloud, and system OEM.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"clean-4\",\n              \"new\": false,\n              \"why\": \"Confirms Vera Rubin production shipments began in August and that major customers have placed purchase orders, supporting the early ramp; it does not establish volume shipments or first revenue recognition by end-FY2027.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e3\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA guided fiscal 2028 revenue growth to about 70%, the first time it has guided a full year ahead; CEO Jensen Huang said demand is much greater than 70% and that supply is what holds the guide there.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"For fiscal 2028, management has guided about 70% revenue growth, the first time it has guided a full year ahead. That guide does not depend on finding more demand. The CEO says demand is much greater than 70%, and that supply is what holds the guide there.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"clean-4\",\n              \"new\": false,\n              \"why\": \"The fiscal 2028 revenue growth guide and the CEO's comment that supply holds the guide bear on the supply-constrained backdrop for Vera Rubin volume shipments; the guide is for fiscal 2028, not a fiscal 2027 shipment forecast.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e4\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA's CFO expects supply to stay a bottleneck at least through the end of fiscal 2028 and called memory pricing extreme.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"The CFO expects supply to stay a bottleneck at least through the end of fiscal 2028 and calls memory pricing extreme.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"clean-4\",\n              \"new\": false,\n              \"why\": \"The CFO's expectation of a supply bottleneck through end-FY2028 is a constraint that could affect whether Vera Rubin reaches volume customer shipments by the end of fiscal 2027.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e5\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA guided fiscal 2028 gross margin to settle in the 72% to 73% range, lower, as memory prices rose more than management expected, partly offset by price increases NVIDIA has already executed.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Gross margin is guided lower. Memory prices have risen more than management expected, and the guide has that margin settling in the 72% to 73% range in fiscal 2028, helped by price increases NVIDIA has already executed.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e6\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA has invested nearly $50 billion in frontier AI labs; management acknowledges some will call this circular financing and says the compute can be redeployed to other customers.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"NVIDIA has invested nearly $50 billion in frontier AI labs. Management concedes some will call this circular financing and says the compute can be redeployed to other customers.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"clean-1\",\n              \"new\": false,\n              \"why\": \"Quantifies NVIDIA's equity investments in frontier AI labs, the equity-investment side of the guarantee/credit-support versus equity-investment comparison in this thesis; it does not report guarantees or credit support.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e7\",\n          \"summary\": \"The 33 analyst estimates for NVIDIA's fiscal 2028 earnings per share range from $12.62 to $17.49 a share.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"The 33 estimates of fiscal 2028 earnings run from $12.62 to $17.49 a share, a wide band for the year the forward multiple is priced on.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e8\",\n          \"summary\": \"Consensus expects NVIDIA's earnings and revenue to grow at a similar pace between fiscal 2027 and fiscal 2028, implying analysts assume profit margins hold roughly steady.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Consensus has earnings and revenue growing at a similar pace between fiscal 2027 and fiscal 2028, so analysts assume profit margins hold roughly steady.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"answer\": \"A21\",\n      \"article\": 4,\n      \"new_questions\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"answer\": \"A22\",\n      \"article\": 5,\n      \"new_questions\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"new-1\",\n          \"question\": \"What revenue growth will Nvidia report for fiscal 2028, and what revenue level does it imply, against the 70% growth the company guided to at its fiscal 2027 second-quarter earnings?\",\n          \"outcome\": \"Nvidia's reported fiscal 2028 revenue growth (and resulting revenue), versus the 70% growth management projected in September 2026 and the ~45% growth analysts had expected before that guidance.\",\n          \"period\": \"Fiscal 2028 (year ending late January 2028); settled by the fiscal 2028 Form 10-K expected around February 2028, per section 3 ([reason] quantity for the next fiscal year, settled by the release of that year's results).\",\n          \"settled_by\": \"Nvidia's fiscal 2028 Form 10-K (annual report) and the quarterly results and guidance that precede it.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"new-2\",\n          \"question\": \"What gross margin will Nvidia report for fiscal 2027, after 75% in the second quarter and analyst estimates of under 72% by the fourth quarter on rising memory-component costs?\",\n          \"outcome\": \"Nvidia's reported fiscal 2027 gross margin versus the 75% second-quarter level and the under-72% fourth-quarter analyst estimate.\",\n          \"period\": \"Fiscal 2027 (year ending late January 2027); settled by the fiscal 2027 Form 10-K expected around February 2027, per section 3 ([reason] quantity for the current fiscal year, settled by the release of that year's results).\",\n          \"settled_by\": \"Nvidia's fiscal 2027 Form 10-K (annual report), which publishes the full-year gross margin.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"kept_statements\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-1\",\n          \"summary\": \"Nvidia's revenue and net income are each expected to grow by roughly 90% or more in its current fiscal year (fiscal 2027), according to estimates cited by the article, even as the stock trades near its lowest valuation in more than a decade.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Nvidia $NVDA stock is trading near its lowest valuation in more than a decade, according to Bloomberg , even as the chipmaker's revenue and net income are each expected to grow by roughly 90% or more in its current fiscal year.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-1\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"The expected ~90% revenue growth in the current fiscal year (fiscal 2027) sets the revenue base from which the guided 70% fiscal 2028 growth would compound, so the estimate informs the fiscal 2028 revenue level; it is an analyst estimate, not company guidance.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-2\",\n          \"summary\": \"Nvidia's gross margin came in at 75% in the quarter before the article ('last quarter', its fiscal 2027 second quarter).\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Nvidia 's gross margin came in at 75% last quarter but analyst estimates compiled by Bloomberg show it sliding under 72% by the fourth quarter, with a recovery expected thereafter.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-2\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"A reported 75% gross margin in the second quarter is the starting level for the full fiscal 2027 annual gross margin the thesis tracks.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-3\",\n          \"summary\": \"Analyst estimates compiled by Bloomberg show Nvidia's gross margin sliding to under 72% by the fourth quarter, with a recovery expected thereafter; the article cites rising costs for key components such as memory chips as a central factor.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"but analyst estimates compiled by Bloomberg show it sliding under 72% by the fourth quarter, with a recovery expected thereafter. Rising costs for key components such as memory chips are a central factor.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-2\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"The estimated slide to under 72% by the fourth quarter, driven by memory-component costs, is a forecast for the path of the fiscal 2027 gross margin the thesis tracks; it is an analyst estimate, not company guidance.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-4\",\n          \"summary\": \"Nvidia guided to 70% revenue growth in fiscal 2028 when it reported second-quarter earnings, well above the 45% analysts had expected at the time.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"the company projected 70% revenue growth in fiscal 2028 — well above the 45% analysts had expected at the time.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-1\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"This is the direct company guidance the thesis is set against: 70% revenue growth for fiscal 2028 versus the 45% consensus beforehand.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-5\",\n          \"summary\": \"Nvidia's revenue more than doubled year over year in the second quarter reported with its second-quarter earnings.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"when revenue more than doubled and the company projected 70% revenue growth in fiscal 2028\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-1\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"The second-quarter revenue doubling informs the fiscal 2027 revenue base off which fiscal 2028's guided 70% growth would be measured; it supports the current-year trajectory, not a fiscal 2028 outcome.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-6\",\n          \"summary\": \"David Russell, global head of market strategy at TradeStation, said Meta Platforms and Alphabet are among the major Nvidia buyers that have moved to design AI chips internally, a shift he believes will gradually erode Nvidia's pricing power and market share.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"David Russell, global head of market strategy at TradeStation, pointed to the growing threat of customers building their own silicon, noting that Meta $META Platforms and Alphabet $GOOGL are among the major Nvidia buyers that have moved to design AI chips internally — a shift he believes will gradually erode Nvidia 's pricing power and market share.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-1\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"A named strategist's view that customer in-house AI silicon will gradually take share is a competitive risk to Nvidia's revenue growth; it is a forecast/opinion, not a reported share loss.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-2\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"The same view attributes gradual erosion of Nvidia's pricing power to customer-built chips, which bears on gross margin, though no figure or timing is given.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"answer\": \"A23\",\n      \"article\": 10,\n      \"new_questions\": [],\n      \"kept_statements\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e1\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA reported fiscal 2027 second-quarter (quarter ended 26 July 2026) revenue of $96.2 billion, up 106% year over year — faster than the fiscal first quarter's 85% year-over-year growth — with the data center business accounting for $89 billion of the total and net income of $59.7 billion, up 126% year over year, according to the company's latest results as reported by fool.com.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Nvidia's latest results make the growth requirement seem nearly routine. Revenue in the fiscal 2027 second quarter (the period ended July 26, 2026) came to $96.2 billion, up 106% over a year earlier. This pace was even faster than the fiscal first quarter's 85% year-over-year growth. The data center business made up $89 billion of the total. And net income , at $59.7 billion, rose 126% year over year.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e2\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA guided fiscal 2027 third-quarter revenue to $108 billion, around 12% above the $96.2 billion reported for fiscal 2027's second quarter, as reported by fool.com.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"The forecasts go far past the quarter. Guidance for the fiscal third quarter is $108 billion in revenue , around 12% above fiscal Q2.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e3\",\n          \"summary\": \"On NVIDIA's late-August 2026 earnings call, CFO Colette Kress said the company expects revenue to rise roughly 70% in fiscal 2028 (the year ending January 2028), calling it \\\"a supply-constrained outlook\\\" — i.e., the limit is manufacturing capacity rather than customer demand, as reported by fool.com.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"And on the company's late-August earnings call, CFO Colette Kress said Nvidia expects revenue to rise roughly 70% in fiscal 2028, the year ending in January 2028. She called it \\\"a supply-constrained outlook.\\\" Put another way, the limit is manufacturing capacity, not customer demand.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"clean-2\",\n              \"new\": false,\n              \"why\": \"The CFO's description of the fiscal 2028 growth outlook as supply-constrained, with manufacturing capacity rather than demand as the limit, is context for how large NVIDIA's purchase and supply commitments (capacity/components/services) may become at the next annual report; it is a management characterization, not a disclosed commitment amount.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e4\",\n          \"summary\": \"On the same late-August 2026 earnings call, NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said gross margins should bottom between 71% and 72% in the fiscal fourth quarter and then settle at 72% to 73% in fiscal 2028 as price hikes kick in, a drop from the 75% gross margin reported for the fiscal 2027 second quarter, as reported by fool.com.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Margins might not change the picture much, either. On the call, Kress said gross margins should bottom between 71% and 72% in the fiscal fourth quarter and then settle at 72% to 73% in fiscal 2028 as price hikes kick in. That'd be a drop from the fiscal second quarter's 75%, though a small one.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e5\",\n          \"summary\": \"Analysts' consensus, as cited by fool.com, had NVIDIA's fiscal 2027 revenue at around $412 billion.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Analysts' consensus already has fiscal 2027 revenue coming in around $412 billion.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"answer\": \"A24\",\n      \"article\": 6,\n      \"new_questions\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"new-1\",\n          \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA's next-generation Vera Rubin data-center platform — the successor generation of the product line that carries the company's data-center value — reach first customer shipments by the end of fiscal 2027?\",\n          \"outcome\": \"First revenue shipments of the Vera Rubin platform, after the company reported it entered full production, confirmed by NVIDIA's own shipment/revenue commentary in quarterly results and SEC filings.\",\n          \"period\": \"NVIDIA fiscal year ending late January 2027 — the current fiscal year-end used as the check date because the item reports full production but gives no shipment date.\",\n          \"settled_by\": \"NVIDIA's quarterly earnings releases and Form 10-Q/10-K filings (data-center platform shipment and revenue commentary) confirming whether Vera Rubin systems shipped to customers within fiscal 2027.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"answer\": \"A25\",\n      \"article\": 7,\n      \"new_questions\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"answer\": \"A26\",\n      \"article\": 8,\n      \"new_questions\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"new-1\",\n          \"question\": \"What total revenue will NVIDIA report for fiscal 2027 (the year ending late January 2027)?\",\n          \"outcome\": \"NVIDIA's fiscal 2027 total revenue, versus the Zacks consensus of $406.05 billion (+88% year over year), given second-quarter fiscal 2027 revenue of $96.22 billion (+106% year over year, Data Center $89.02 billion, +117%) and third-quarter guidance of $108 billion +/- 2%.\",\n          \"period\": \"Fiscal year 2027 (ending late January 2027); settled at NVIDIA's fiscal 2027 fourth-quarter results and Form 10-K, expected around February 2027.\",\n          \"settled_by\": \"NVIDIA's fiscal 2027 fourth-quarter and full-year results release and its fiscal 2027 Form 10-K (annual report), expected around February 2027.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"kept_statements\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e1\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA reported second-quarter fiscal 2027 revenue of $96.22 billion, up 106% year over year, with Data Center revenue up 117% to $89.02 billion.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"NVIDIA generated $96.22 billion in second-quarter fiscal 2027 revenues, up 106% year over year, while Data Center revenues surged 117% to $89.02 billion.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-1\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"Reported quarterly revenue and year-over-year growth set the base for the fiscal 2027 full-year revenue question; Data Center is the segment that carries the total.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e2\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA guided third-quarter fiscal 2027 revenue to $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, which the article says implies 89.5% year-over-year growth and a 12.2% sequential increase.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"The company expects third-quarter revenues of $108 billion (+/- 2%), indicating 89.5% year-over-year growth and a 12.2% sequential increase.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-1\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"Company guidance for the next quarter is a direct input to the fiscal 2027 full-year revenue outcome.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e3\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA said it expects fiscal 2028 revenue growth of about 70%, while cautioning that supply constraints could limit how quickly it meets demand.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"NVIDIA also expects fiscal 2028 revenue growth of about 70%, although supply constraints could limit how quickly it meets demand.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-1\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"Management's own next-year growth expectation frames the durability of the revenue path beyond fiscal 2027; it is not a fiscal 2027 figure and is not treated as one.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e4\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA had committed $279 billion to secure supply and production capacity at the end of the second quarter of fiscal 2027, up from $119 billion at the end of the first quarter, with most commitments tied to memory and manufacturing facilities needed for current and future data center products.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"At the end of the second quarter of fiscal 2027, the company had committed $279 billion to secure supply and production capacity, up from $119 billion in the first quarter. Most commitments are tied to memory and manufacturing facilities needed for current and future data center products.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"clean-2\",\n              \"new\": false,\n              \"why\": \"Directly reports the quantity clean-2 tracks (purchase and supply commitments), here at the end of Q2 fiscal 2027 rather than at the annual report date; shows the quarter-on-quarter increase from $119 billion and that most of it is memory and manufacturing capacity.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e5\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA's next-generation Vera Rubin platform began production shipments in the third quarter (of fiscal 2027), per the article.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Vera Rubin began production shipments in the third quarter.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"clean-4\",\n              \"new\": false,\n              \"why\": \"Reports that Vera Rubin has moved into production shipments in the third quarter, a step toward the volume customer shipments and first revenue that clean-4 tracks within fiscal 2027; does not establish volume or revenue recognition.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-1\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"Vera Rubin shipments beginning in Q3 fiscal 2027 are a revenue driver inside the fiscal 2027 period covered by the total-revenue question.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e6\",\n          \"summary\": \"Advanced Micro Devices reported second-quarter 2026 Data Center revenue of $6.7 billion, up 107% year over year, with Instinct accelerator sales more than doubling.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"In the second quarter of 2026, AMD's Data Center revenues rose 107% year over year to $6.7 billion, while Instinct sales more than doubled.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e7\",\n          \"summary\": \"AMD said its Helios rack-scale platform is in production, with initial shipments expected late in the third quarter of 2026 and a larger ramp-up in the fourth quarter and 2027.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Helios is in production, with initial shipments expected late in the third quarter and a larger ramp-up in the fourth quarter and 2027.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e8\",\n          \"summary\": \"Anthropic plans to deploy up to 2 gigawatts of AMD MI450-series GPUs using the AMD Helios rack-scale platform, with the first gigawatt beginning in the first half of 2027.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Anthropic plans to deploy up to 2 gigawatts of MI450-series GPUs using the AMD Helios rack-scale platform, with the first gigawatt beginning in the first half of 2027.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e9\",\n          \"summary\": \"Microsoft plans to deploy AMD's Helios rack-scale platform at scale on Azure.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Microsoft plans to deploy Helios at scale on Azure.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e10\",\n          \"summary\": \"AMD expects its Data Center segment revenue to more than double year over year in 2027.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Advanced Micro Devices expects Data Center segment revenues to more than double year over year in 2027.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e11\",\n          \"summary\": \"Intel reported second-quarter 2026 revenue of $16.13 billion, up 25%, with Data Center and AI revenue up 59% to $6.26 billion.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Its second-quarter revenues rose 25% to $16.13 billion, while Data Center and AI revenues surged 59% to $6.26 billion.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e12\",\n          \"summary\": \"Intel's purpose-built silicon revenue rose about 20% sequentially in the second quarter of 2026 and nearly tripled year over year.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"In the second quarter of 2026, purpose-built silicon revenues increased about 20% sequentially and nearly tripled year over year.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e13\",\n          \"summary\": \"On its last earnings call, Intel management said purpose-built silicon revenue is approaching an estimated $2 billion run rate and that the company is targeting $4 billion in the near future.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"During the last earnings call, management noted that purpose-built silicon revenues are approaching an estimated $2 billion run rate, and the company is targeting $4 billion in the near future.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e14\",\n          \"summary\": \"The Zacks Consensus Estimate put NVIDIA's fiscal 2027 revenue at $406.05 billion, an 88% year-over-year increase.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"The Zacks Consensus Estimate for fiscal 2027 revenues is currently pegged at $406.05 billion, indicating an 88% year-over-year increase.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-1\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"The consensus figure is the benchmark against which the fiscal 2027 total-revenue outcome will be judged.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e15\",\n          \"summary\": \"The Zacks Consensus Estimate implies NVIDIA's earnings will grow about 93.9% year over year in fiscal 2027 and 65.8% in fiscal 2028, and the consensus estimates for both fiscal years were revised upward over the past 30 days.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"The Zacks Consensus Estimate for NVIDIA's fiscal 2027 and 2028 earnings implies a year-over-year increase of approximately 93.9% and 65.8%, respectively. Estimates for fiscal 2027 and 2028 have been revised upward over the past 30 days.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"answer\": \"A27\",\n      \"article\": 7,\n      \"new_questions\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"answer\": \"A28\",\n      \"article\": 9,\n      \"new_questions\": [],\n      \"kept_statements\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-1\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA management says Vera Rubin, its newest AI platform, should be the fastest product ramp in the company's history, and production shipments of the platform began in August, with purchase orders already received from every major hyperscaler, AI cloud provider and system OEM, according to Trefis's 24 September 2026 article.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"NVIDIA expects Vera Rubin, its newest platform, to be the fastest product ramp in the company’s history.\",\n            \"Production shipments began in August, with purchase orders already in from every major hyperscaler, AI cloud, and system OEM.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"clean-4\",\n              \"new\": false,\n              \"why\": \"Reports that Vera Rubin production shipments began in August with orders from every major hyperscaler, a direct step toward the volume customer shipments/revenue recognition clean-4 asks about; the 'fastest ramp' expectation is management's characterization, not a shipment date.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-2\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA management puts the company's revenue opportunity at about $40 billion per gigawatt of capacity with Vera Rubin, against $25 billion per gigawatt with Blackwell, per Trefis.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Management puts NVIDIA’s revenue opportunity at about $40 billion per gigawatt of capacity with Vera Rubin, against $25 billion with Blackwell.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"clean-4\",\n              \"new\": false,\n              \"why\": \"Quantifies the revenue value management attaches to each gigawatt of Vera Rubin capacity, framing the commercial significance of the ramp whose shipment timing clean-4 tracks; it does not establish shipment timing or revenue recognition itself.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-3\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA management guided about 70% revenue growth for fiscal 2028, the first time it has given a full-year-ahead guide; the CEO said demand is much greater than 70% and that supply is what holds the guide at that level, according to Trefis.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"For fiscal 2028, management has guided about 70% revenue growth, the first time it has guided a full year ahead.\",\n            \"That guide does not depend on finding more demand. The CEO says demand is much greater than 70%, and that supply is what holds the guide there.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-4\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA's CFO expects supply to remain a bottleneck at least through the end of fiscal 2028 and calls memory pricing extreme, according to Trefis.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"The CFO expects supply to stay a bottleneck at least through the end of fiscal 2028 and calls memory pricing extreme.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-5\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA guided its gross margin lower, to settle in the 72% to 73% range in fiscal 2028, because memory prices have risen more than management expected, partly offset by price increases NVIDIA has already executed, according to Trefis.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Gross margin is guided lower. Memory prices have risen more than management expected, and the guide has that margin settling in the 72% to 73% range in fiscal 2028, helped by price increases NVIDIA has already executed.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-6\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA has invested nearly $50 billion in frontier AI labs; management concedes some will call this circular financing and says the compute can be redeployed to other customers, according to Trefis.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Some of that demand also leans on NVIDIA’s own balance sheet. NVIDIA has invested nearly $50 billion in frontier AI labs. Management concedes some will call this circular financing and says the compute can be redeployed to other customers.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"clean-1\",\n              \"new\": false,\n              \"why\": \"Gives the scale of NVIDIA's equity investment in frontier AI labs (nearly $50 billion), the figure clean-1 explicitly compares with disclosed credit support and minimum-revenue guarantees at the next annual report; the item does not quantify any guarantee or backstop.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-7\",\n          \"summary\": \"The 33 analyst estimates of NVIDIA's fiscal 2028 earnings range from $12.62 to $17.49 a share — a wide band for the year the forward multiple is priced on, according to Trefis.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"The 33 estimates of fiscal 2028 earnings run from $12.62 to $17.49 a share, a wide band for the year the forward multiple is priced on.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"answer\": \"A29\",\n      \"article\": 10,\n      \"new_questions\": [],\n      \"kept_statements\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev1\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA reported fiscal 2027 second-quarter (quarter ended July 26, 2026) revenue of $96.2 billion, up 106% year over year, faster than the fiscal first quarter's 85% growth; the data center business accounted for $89 billion of the total, and net income was $59.7 billion, up 126% year over year. Reported by fool.com (Daniel Sparks) citing NVIDIA's results.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Nvidia's latest results make the growth requirement seem nearly routine. Revenue in the fiscal 2027 second quarter (the period ended July 26, 2026) came to $96.2 billion, up 106% over a year earlier. This pace was even faster than the fiscal first quarter's 85% year-over-year growth. The data center business made up $89 billion of the total. And net income , at $59.7 billion, rose 126% year over year.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev2\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA guided fiscal 2027 third-quarter revenue to $108 billion, about 12% above second-quarter revenue, according to the article.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Guidance for the fiscal third quarter is $108 billion in revenue , around 12% above fiscal Q2.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev3\",\n          \"summary\": \"On NVIDIA's late-August 2026 earnings call, CFO Colette Kress said the company expects revenue to rise roughly 70% in fiscal 2028 (the year ending January 2028), calling it \\\"a supply-constrained outlook\\\" in which the limit is manufacturing capacity, not customer demand.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"And on the company's late-August earnings call, CFO Colette Kress said Nvidia expects revenue to rise roughly 70% in fiscal 2028, the year ending in January 2028. She called it \\\"a supply-constrained outlook.\\\" Put another way, the limit is manufacturing capacity, not customer demand.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"clean-2\",\n              \"new\": false,\n              \"why\": \"The CFO frames the fiscal 2028 outlook as constrained by manufacturing capacity rather than demand, which bears on how much NVIDIA may need to commit to purchasing capacity, components or services; the item gives no commitment amounts.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev4\",\n          \"summary\": \"On the earnings call, NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said gross margins should bottom between 71% and 72% in the fiscal fourth quarter and then settle at 72% to 73% in fiscal 2028 as price increases take effect, down from 75% in the fiscal second quarter.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"On the call, Kress said gross margins should bottom between 71% and 72% in the fiscal fourth quarter and then settle at 72% to 73% in fiscal 2028 as price hikes kick in. That'd be a drop from the fiscal second quarter's 75%, though a small one.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev5\",\n          \"summary\": \"Analysts' consensus had NVIDIA's fiscal 2027 revenue at around $412 billion, according to the article.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Analysts' consensus already has fiscal 2027 revenue coming in around $412 billion.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"answer\": \"A30\",\n      \"article\": 8,\n      \"new_questions\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"new-fy2027-total-revenue\",\n          \"question\": \"What total revenue will NVIDIA report for fiscal 2027?\",\n          \"outcome\": \"NVIDIA's total revenue for fiscal 2027, compared with the $96.22 billion reported in Q2 fiscal 2027, the $108 billion Q3 fiscal 2027 guidance and the $406.05 billion Zacks Consensus Estimate.\",\n          \"period\": \"Fiscal 2027 (year ending late January 2027), settled by NVIDIA's FY2027 Form 10-K expected around February 2027.\",\n          \"settled_by\": \"NVIDIA's FY2027 Form 10-K and quarterly results, expected around February 2027.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"new-fy2028-revenue-growth\",\n          \"question\": \"What year-over-year revenue growth will NVIDIA report for fiscal 2028?\",\n          \"outcome\": \"NVIDIA's total revenue growth for fiscal 2028, compared with the company's expectation of about 70% growth.\",\n          \"period\": \"Fiscal 2028 (year ending late January 2028), settled by NVIDIA's FY2028 Form 10-K expected around February 2028.\",\n          \"settled_by\": \"NVIDIA's FY2028 Form 10-K and quarterly results, expected around February 2028.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"kept_statements\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e1_279b_commitments\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA reported that, at the end of Q2 fiscal 2027, it had committed $279 billion to secure supply and production capacity, up from $119 billion at the end of Q1 fiscal 2027. Most of the commitments are tied to memory and manufacturing facilities needed for current and future data center products.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"At the end of the second quarter of fiscal 2027, the company had committed $279 billion to secure supply and production capacity, up from $119 billion in the first quarter. Most commitments are tied to memory and manufacturing facilities needed for current and future data center products.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"clean-2\",\n              \"new\": false,\n              \"why\": \"Directly states the amount of NVIDIA's supply and production capacity commitments at the end of Q2 fiscal 2027 and the prior-quarter comparison, which is the quantity clean-2 tracks at the next annual report.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e2_q2_fy2027_revenue\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA reported Q2 fiscal 2027 revenue of $96.22 billion, up 106% year over year, including Data Center revenue of $89.02 billion, up 117%.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"NVIDIA generated $96.22 billion in second-quarter fiscal 2027 revenues, up 106% year over year, while Data Center revenues surged 117% to $89.02 billion.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-fy2027-total-revenue\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"Reports NVIDIA's Q2 fiscal 2027 total revenue and Data Center revenue, direct inputs to the fiscal 2027 annual revenue outcome.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e3_q3_fy2027_guidance\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA guided Q3 fiscal 2027 revenue to $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, implying 89.5% year-over-year growth and a 12.2% sequential increase.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"The company expects third-quarter revenues of $108 billion (+/- 2%), indicating 89.5% year-over-year growth and a 12.2% sequential increase.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-fy2027-total-revenue\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"Company guidance for Q3 fiscal 2027 revenue, a direct input to the fiscal 2027 annual revenue outcome.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e4_vera_rubin_shipments\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA's next-generation Vera Rubin platform began production shipments in Q3 fiscal 2027, according to the article.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Vera Rubin began production shipments in the third quarter.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"clean-4\",\n              \"new\": false,\n              \"why\": \"States Vera Rubin began production shipments in Q3 fiscal 2027, evidence on the product milestone clean-4 tracks (volume shipments/first revenue by end fiscal 2027). It does not by itself establish volume or revenue recognition.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e5_fy2028_revenue_growth_guidance\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA expects fiscal 2028 revenue growth of about 70%, although supply constraints could limit how quickly it meets demand.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"NVIDIA also expects fiscal 2028 revenue growth of about 70%, although supply constraints could limit how quickly it meets demand.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-fy2028-revenue-growth\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"Company expectation for fiscal 2028 revenue growth of about 70%, the outcome tracked by this thesis.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e6_zacks_fy2027_revenue\",\n          \"summary\": \"The Zacks Consensus Estimate for NVIDIA's fiscal 2027 revenue is $406.05 billion, implying an 88% year-over-year increase.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"The Zacks Consensus Estimate for fiscal 2027 revenues is currently pegged at $406.05 billion, indicating an 88% year-over-year increase.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-fy2027-total-revenue\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"Third-party consensus estimate for fiscal 2027 total revenue, an input to the fiscal 2027 revenue question.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e7_zacks_fy2027_fy2028_eps\",\n          \"summary\": \"The Zacks Consensus Estimate implies NVIDIA's fiscal 2027 and fiscal 2028 earnings will grow approximately 93.9% and 65.8% year over year, respectively; Zacks says estimates for both years were revised upward over the past 30 days.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"The Zacks Consensus Estimate for NVIDIA's fiscal 2027 and 2028 earnings implies a year-over-year increase of approximately 93.9% and 65.8%, respectively. Estimates for fiscal 2027 and 2028 have been revised upward over the past 30 days.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e8_amd_q2_2026_dc_revenue\",\n          \"summary\": \"AMD reported Q2 2026 Data Center revenue of $6.7 billion, up 107% year over year, and said Instinct sales more than doubled.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"In the second quarter of 2026, AMD's Data Center revenues rose 107% year over year to $6.7 billion, while Instinct sales more than doubled.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-fy2028-revenue-growth\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"AMD's reported data center AI revenue growth and doubling of Instinct sales show competitive momentum in NVIDIA's main market, relevant to NVIDIA's fiscal 2028 revenue growth outlook.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e9_amd_helios_production\",\n          \"summary\": \"AMD said its Helios rack-scale platform is in production, with initial shipments expected late in the third quarter and a larger ramp-up in the fourth quarter and 2027.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Helios is in production, with initial shipments expected late in the third quarter and a larger ramp-up in the fourth quarter and 2027.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-fy2028-revenue-growth\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"AMD's Helios platform entering production and ramping in Q3/Q4 2026 and 2027 is competitive evidence that could affect NVIDIA's fiscal 2028 revenue growth.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e10_anthropic_amd_deployment\",\n          \"summary\": \"Anthropic plans to deploy up to 2 gigawatts of AMD MI450-series GPUs using AMD's Helios rack-scale platform, with the first gigawatt beginning in the first half of 2027.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Anthropic plans to deploy up to 2 gigawatts of MI450-series GPUs using the AMD Helios rack-scale platform, with the first gigawatt beginning in the first half of 2027.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-fy2028-revenue-growth\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"Anthropic's planned 2 gigawatt MI450 deployment on AMD Helios, with first 1 gigawatt in H1 2027, is a large customer commitment to a competing AI platform, relevant to NVIDIA's fiscal 2028 growth outlook.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e11_microsoft_amd_helios\",\n          \"summary\": \"Microsoft plans to deploy AMD's Helios platform at scale on Azure.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Microsoft plans to deploy Helios at scale on Azure.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-fy2028-revenue-growth\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"Microsoft's plan to deploy AMD Helios at scale on Azure is a hyperscaler commitment to a competing platform, relevant to NVIDIA's fiscal 2028 revenue growth outlook.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e12_amd_dc_guidance_2027\",\n          \"summary\": \"AMD expects its Data Center segment revenues to more than double year over year in 2027.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Advanced Micro Devices expects Data Center segment revenues to more than double year over year in 2027.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-fy2028-revenue-growth\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"AMD's expectation that data center segment revenue will more than double in 2027 signals competitive pressure in NVIDIA's main market, relevant to fiscal 2028 revenue growth.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e13_intel_q2_2026_revenue\",\n          \"summary\": \"Intel reported Q2 2026 revenue of $16.13 billion, up 25%, including Data Center and AI revenue of $6.26 billion, up 59%.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Its second-quarter revenues rose 25% to $16.13 billion, while Data Center and AI revenues surged 59% to $6.26 billion.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-fy2028-revenue-growth\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"Intel's reported Data Center and AI revenue growth shows another competitor expanding in AI infrastructure, relevant to NVIDIA's fiscal 2028 revenue growth outlook.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e14_intel_purpose_built_actual\",\n          \"summary\": \"Intel reported that Q2 2026 purpose-built silicon revenues increased about 20% sequentially and nearly tripled year over year.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"In the second quarter of 2026, purpose-built silicon revenues increased about 20% sequentially and nearly tripled year over year.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-fy2028-revenue-growth\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"Intel's reported purpose-built silicon revenue growth shows competitive custom-silicon momentum, relevant to NVIDIA's fiscal 2028 revenue growth outlook.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e15_intel_purpose_built_outlook\",\n          \"summary\": \"On its last earnings call, Intel management said purpose-built silicon revenues are approaching an estimated $2 billion run rate and that the company is targeting $4 billion in the near future.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"During the last earnings call, management noted that purpose-built silicon revenues are approaching an estimated $2 billion run rate, and the company is targeting $4 billion in the near future.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-fy2028-revenue-growth\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"Intel's ~$2 billion run rate and $4 billion target for purpose-built silicon signal competitive custom-silicon ambition, relevant to NVIDIA's fiscal 2028 revenue growth outlook.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"answer\": \"A31\",\n      \"article\": 8,\n      \"new_questions\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"nvda-fy2027-total-revenue\",\n          \"question\": \"How much total revenue will NVIDIA report for fiscal 2027, the year that carries the business?\",\n          \"outcome\": \"NVIDIA's reported total revenue for fiscal year 2027 (year ending late January 2027), judged against the Zacks consensus of $406.05 billion and the run-rate implied by $96.22 billion of second-quarter revenue and $108 billion third-quarter guidance.\",\n          \"period\": \"Fiscal 2027 (year ending late January 2027); settled by NVIDIA's fourth-quarter and full-year fiscal 2027 results and Form 10-K, expected around February 2027 — the release of that fiscal year's results, per section 3 for a [reason] quantity.\",\n          \"settled_by\": \"NVIDIA's fourth-quarter and full-year fiscal 2027 earnings release and Form 10-K, which report total revenue for the fiscal year.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"kept_statements\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e1-supply-commitments\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA reported that at the end of the second quarter of fiscal 2027 it had committed $279 billion to secure supply and production capacity, up from $119 billion at the end of the first quarter, with most commitments tied to memory and manufacturing facilities needed for current and future data center products.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"At the end of the second quarter of fiscal 2027, the company had committed $279 billion to secure supply and production capacity, up from $119 billion in the first quarter. Most commitments are tied to memory and manufacturing facilities needed for current and future data center products.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"clean-2\",\n              \"new\": false,\n              \"why\": \"Directly gives the size of NVIDIA's supply and production capacity commitments ($279 billion, up from $119 billion), the quantity clean-2 tracks at the next annual report; this is a quarter-end disclosure, not the annual-report figure.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e2-q2-fy2027-revenue\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA reported second-quarter fiscal 2027 revenue of $96.22 billion, up 106% year over year, with Data Center revenue up 117% to $89.02 billion.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"NVIDIA generated $96.22 billion in second-quarter fiscal 2027 revenues, up 106% year over year, while Data Center revenues surged 117% to $89.02 billion.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"nvda-fy2027-total-revenue\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"Actual quarterly revenue and data-center revenue for fiscal 2027 bear directly on the fiscal-year total this thesis tracks, and on the growth rate needed to reach the current consensus.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e3-q3-fy2027-guidance\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA guided third-quarter fiscal 2027 revenue to $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, which the article says implies 89.5% year-over-year growth and a 12.2% sequential increase.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"The company expects third-quarter revenues of $108 billion (+/- 2%), indicating 89.5% year-over-year growth and a 12.2% sequential increase.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"nvda-fy2027-total-revenue\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"Company guidance for one fiscal 2027 quarter is a component of the fiscal-year revenue total this thesis tracks and anchors the path to consensus.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e4-vera-rubin-production-shipments\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA's next-generation Vera Rubin AI platform began production shipments in the third quarter of fiscal 2027, the article reports.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Vera Rubin began production shipments in the third quarter.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"clean-4\",\n              \"new\": false,\n              \"why\": \"Reports that Vera Rubin has moved into production shipments within fiscal 2027, evidence that the platform is progressing from full production toward the volume customer shipments and first revenue recognition clean-4 tracks; the item gives no volume, customer or revenue-recognition figure.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e5-fy2028-revenue-growth-outlook\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA expects fiscal 2028 revenue growth of about 70%, the article reports, adding that supply constraints could limit how quickly it meets demand.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"NVIDIA also expects fiscal 2028 revenue growth of about 70%, although supply constraints could limit how quickly it meets demand.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e6-zacks-fy2027-revenue-consensus\",\n          \"summary\": \"The Zacks Consensus Estimate for NVIDIA's fiscal 2027 revenue is $406.05 billion, implying an 88% year-over-year increase, Zacks reported.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"The Zacks Consensus Estimate for fiscal 2027 revenues is currently pegged at $406.05 billion, indicating an 88% year-over-year increase.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"nvda-fy2027-total-revenue\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"Names the consensus level for the exact quantity this thesis tracks, setting the bar against which NVIDIA's reported fiscal 2027 revenue is judged.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e7-amd-q2-2026-data-center-revenue\",\n          \"summary\": \"AMD's Data Center revenue rose 107% year over year to $6.7 billion in the second quarter of 2026, with Instinct accelerator sales more than doubling, the article reports.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"In the second quarter of 2026, AMD's Data Center revenues rose 107% year over year to $6.7 billion, while Instinct sales more than doubled.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"nvda-fy2027-total-revenue\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"Competitor's reported AI data-center growth (Instinct sales more than doubling) is evidence of competitive pressure on NVIDIA's data-center revenue path; the item does not quantify any share shift.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e8-amd-helios-shipment-plan\",\n          \"summary\": \"AMD's Helios rack-scale AI platform is in production, with initial shipments expected late in the third quarter of 2026 and a larger ramp-up in the fourth quarter and 2027, the article reports.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Helios is in production, with initial shipments expected late in the third quarter and a larger ramp-up in the fourth quarter and 2027.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"nvda-fy2027-total-revenue\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"A competing rack-scale platform entering shipment is competitive evidence for NVIDIA's data-center revenue path; the plan does not establish orders taken from NVIDIA.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e9-anthropic-mi450-deployment\",\n          \"summary\": \"Anthropic plans to deploy up to 2 gigawatts of AMD MI450-series GPUs using AMD's Helios rack-scale platform, with the first gigawatt beginning in the first half of 2027.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Anthropic plans to deploy up to 2 gigawatts of MI450-series GPUs using the AMD Helios rack-scale platform, with the first gigawatt beginning in the first half of 2027.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"nvda-fy2027-total-revenue\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"A named large AI customer committing up to 2 gigawatts to a competitor's accelerators is demand-side competitive evidence for NVIDIA's revenue path; it is a plan, not a reported loss of NVIDIA orders.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e10-microsoft-helios-azure\",\n          \"summary\": \"Microsoft plans to deploy AMD's Helios platform at scale on Azure, the article reports.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Microsoft plans to deploy Helios at scale on Azure.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"nvda-fy2027-total-revenue\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"A named hyperscaler planning at-scale deployment of a competing AI platform bears on competitive pressure on NVIDIA's data-center revenue; no volume or timing is given.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e11-amd-2027-data-center-outlook\",\n          \"summary\": \"AMD expects its Data Center segment revenues to more than double year over year in 2027.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Advanced Micro Devices expects Data Center segment revenues to more than double year over year in 2027.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"nvda-fy2027-total-revenue\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"A competitor's forecast of more than doubling data-center revenue in 2027 is competitive evidence bearing on NVIDIA's revenue growth path beyond fiscal 2027; it is AMD's forecast, not a share calculation.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e12-intel-q2-2026-revenue\",\n          \"summary\": \"Intel's second-quarter 2026 revenue rose 25% to $16.13 billion, with Data Center and AI revenue up 59% to $6.26 billion, the article reports.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Its second-quarter revenues rose 25% to $16.13 billion, while Data Center and AI revenues surged 59% to $6.26 billion.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"nvda-fy2027-total-revenue\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"A second competitor's reported AI data-center growth is evidence of a broadening competitive field in AI infrastructure that bears on NVIDIA's revenue path; the measure includes CPUs and no accelerator share data is given.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e13-intel-purpose-built-silicon\",\n          \"summary\": \"Intel management said on its last earnings call that purpose-built silicon revenue, which rose about 20% sequentially and nearly tripled year over year in the second quarter of 2026, is approaching an estimated $2 billion run rate, with the company targeting $4 billion in the near future.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"In the second quarter of 2026, purpose-built silicon revenues increased about 20% sequentially and nearly tripled year over year. During the last earnings call, management noted that purpose-built silicon revenues are approaching an estimated $2 billion run rate, and the company is targeting $4 billion in the near future.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"nvda-fy2027-total-revenue\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"Custom purpose-built silicon is the ASIC route that competes with NVIDIA's merchant accelerators; its stated run rate and target are competitive evidence bearing on NVIDIA's revenue path, though the figure covers Intel's whole custom-silicon business.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e14-zacks-eps-consensus-and-revisions\",\n          \"summary\": \"The Zacks Consensus Estimate implies NVIDIA's fiscal 2027 and fiscal 2028 earnings will rise approximately 93.9% and 65.8% year over year respectively, and estimates for both years were revised upward over the past 30 days, Zacks reported.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"The Zacks Consensus Estimate for NVIDIA's fiscal 2027 and 2028 earnings implies a year-over-year increase of approximately 93.9% and 65.8%, respectively. Estimates for fiscal 2027 and 2028 have been revised upward over the past 30 days.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"answer\": \"A32\",\n      \"article\": 4,\n      \"new_questions\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"answer\": \"A33\",\n      \"article\": 3,\n      \"new_questions\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"answer\": \"A34\",\n      \"article\": 6,\n      \"new_questions\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"new-1\",\n          \"question\": \"Will NVIDIA's Vera Rubin platform — the next-generation data-center GPU system that carries the company's value — reach first customer shipments (revenue-generating deliveries) by the end of fiscal 2027?\",\n          \"outcome\": \"Whether NVIDIA confirms first customer shipments, and revenue, from Vera Rubin systems; the item reports the platform entered full production in the period covered by the Aug. 26, 2026 press release (fiscal Q2 2027).\",\n          \"period\": \"NVIDIA fiscal year ending late January 2027 — the current fiscal year-end used as the check date, since the item reports full-production entry but gives no shipment date of its own.\",\n          \"settled_by\": \"NVIDIA quarterly earnings releases, prepared remarks and Form 10-Q/10-K disclosures confirming first shipments or recognized revenue from Vera Rubin systems (each quarterly report through fiscal 2027 provides a check point).\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"answer\": \"A35\",\n      \"article\": 2,\n      \"new_questions\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"new-fy27-revenue\",\n          \"question\": \"What total revenue will NVIDIA report for its current fiscal year (fiscal 2027, ending late January 2027), versus the Zacks consensus of $406.05 billion (+88% year over year) as of 22 September 2026?\",\n          \"outcome\": \"NVIDIA's reported total revenue for fiscal 2027 and its growth versus fiscal 2026, compared with the consensus estimate of $406.05 billion (+88%).\",\n          \"period\": \"Fiscal 2027 (year ending late January 2027); settled by the release of NVIDIA's fiscal 2027 fourth-quarter and full-year results, expected around February 2027 — the release of that fiscal year's results, per section 3 ([reason]).\",\n          \"settled_by\": \"NVIDIA's fiscal 2027 fourth-quarter and full-year results release and Form 10-K, expected around February 2027.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"new-fy28-revenue\",\n          \"question\": \"What total revenue will NVIDIA report for its next fiscal year (fiscal 2028, ending late January 2028), versus the Zacks consensus of $671.95 billion (+65.5%) as of 22 September 2026?\",\n          \"outcome\": \"NVIDIA's reported total revenue for fiscal 2028 and its growth versus fiscal 2027, compared with the consensus estimate of $671.95 billion (+65.5%).\",\n          \"period\": \"Fiscal 2028 (year ending late January 2028); settled by the release of NVIDIA's fiscal 2028 fourth-quarter and full-year results, expected around February 2029 — the release of that fiscal year's results, per section 3 ([reason]).\",\n          \"settled_by\": \"NVIDIA's fiscal 2028 fourth-quarter and full-year results release and Form 10-K, expected around February 2029.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"kept_statements\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-q-eps\",\n          \"summary\": \"Zacks' consensus estimate expects NVIDIA to report earnings of $2.47 per share in the current quarter (the quarter current as of the 22 September 2026 article), a change of +90% from the year-ago quarter; the Zacks Consensus Estimate for that quarter has risen 5.8% over the last 30 days.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"For the current quarter, Nvidia is expected to post earnings of $2.47 per share, indicating a change of +90% from the year-ago quarter. The Zacks Consensus Estimate has changed +5.8% over the last 30 days.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-fy27-eps\",\n          \"summary\": \"Zacks' consensus earnings estimate for NVIDIA's current fiscal year (fiscal 2027, ending late January 2027) is $9.25 per share, a change of +93.9% from the prior year, and the estimate has risen 5.1% over the last 30 days.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"For the current fiscal year, the consensus earnings estimate of $9.25 points to a change of +93.9% from the prior year. Over the last 30 days, this estimate has changed +5.1%.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-fy28-eps\",\n          \"summary\": \"Zacks' consensus earnings estimate for NVIDIA's next fiscal year (fiscal 2028, ending late January 2028) is $15.33 per share, a change of +65.8% from what NVIDIA is expected to report a year earlier, and the estimate has risen 21.8% over the past month.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"For the next fiscal year, the consensus earnings estimate of $15.33 indicates a change of +65.8% from what Nvidia is expected to report a year ago. Over the past month, the estimate has changed +21.8%.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-q-sales\",\n          \"summary\": \"Zacks' consensus sales estimate for NVIDIA's current quarter (the quarter current as of the 22 September 2026 article) is $109.02 billion, a year-over-year change of +91.2%.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"For Nvidia, the consensus sales estimate for the current quarter of $109.02 billion indicates a year-over-year change of +91.2%.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-fy27-revenue\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"The source states a current-quarter consensus sales estimate of $109.02 billion (+91.2% year over year). It is the quarterly run-rate that feeds the fiscal 2027 total; inference only — it does not establish the full-year revenue, and the item gives no line of sight beyond the current quarter.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-annual-sales\",\n          \"summary\": \"Zacks' consensus sales estimates for NVIDIA are $406.05 billion for the current fiscal year (fiscal 2027) and $671.95 billion for the next fiscal year (fiscal 2028), indicating changes of +88% and +65.5% respectively.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"For Nvidia, the consensus sales estimate for the current quarter of $109.02 billion indicates a year-over-year change of +91.2%. For the current and next fiscal years, $406.05 billion and $671.95 billion estimates indicate +88% and +65.5% changes, respectively.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-fy27-revenue\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"The source states the consensus estimate for NVIDIA's fiscal 2027 total revenue at $406.05 billion (+88%); this is the level the thesis tracks. It is an estimate, not reported revenue.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-fy28-revenue\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"The source states the consensus estimate for NVIDIA's fiscal 2028 total revenue at $671.95 billion (+65.5%), the level the thesis tracks for the next fiscal year. It is an estimate, not reported revenue.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"answer\": \"A36\",\n      \"article\": 9,\n      \"new_questions\": [],\n      \"kept_statements\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev1\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA management says Vera Rubin, its newest AI platform, carries a revenue opportunity of about $40 billion per gigawatt of capacity versus about $25 billion per gigawatt with Blackwell, and expects Vera Rubin to be the fastest product ramp in the company's history, according to Trefis.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"NVIDIA expects Vera Rubin, its newest platform, to be the fastest product ramp in the company’s history. Management puts NVIDIA’s revenue opportunity at about $40 billion per gigawatt of capacity with Vera Rubin, against $25 billion with Blackwell.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"clean-4\",\n              \"new\": false,\n              \"why\": \"Management's per-gigawatt revenue-opportunity figures for Vera Rubin versus Blackwell bear on the size and economics of the Vera Rubin ramp the thesis tracks, though they are not shipment or revenue-recognition figures.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev2\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA began production shipments of its Vera Rubin platform in August, with purchase orders already received from every major hyperscaler, AI cloud and system OEM, according to the company as reported by Trefis.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Production shipments began in August, with purchase orders already in from every major hyperscaler, AI cloud, and system OEM.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"clean-4\",\n              \"new\": false,\n              \"why\": \"Reports that Vera Rubin production shipments began in August 2026 with purchase orders from all major hyperscalers, a direct step toward the volume customer shipments and first revenue that thesis tracks.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev3\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA management guided fiscal 2028 revenue growth of about 70%, the first time it has given a full-year guide; CEO says demand is much greater than 70% and that supply is what holds the guide there, while the CFO expects supply to stay a bottleneck at least through the end of fiscal 2028 and calls memory pricing extreme.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"For fiscal 2028, management has guided about 70% revenue growth, the first time it has guided a full year ahead. That guide does not depend on finding more demand. The CEO says demand is much greater than 70%, and that supply is what holds the guide there. The CFO expects supply to stay a bottleneck at least through the end of fiscal 2028 and calls memory pricing extreme.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev4\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA guided its gross margin to settle in the 72% to 73% range in fiscal 2028, lower as memory costs climb; memory prices have risen more than management expected, partly offset by price increases NVIDIA has already executed, according to Trefis.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Gross margin is guided lower. Memory prices have risen more than management expected, and the guide has that margin settling in the 72% to 73% range in fiscal 2028, helped by price increases NVIDIA has already executed.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev5\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA has invested nearly $50 billion in frontier AI labs; management acknowledges some will call this circular financing and says the compute can be redeployed to other customers, according to Trefis.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Some of that demand also leans on NVIDIA’s own balance sheet. NVIDIA has invested nearly $50 billion in frontier AI labs. Management concedes some will call this circular financing and says the compute can be redeployed to other customers.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"clean-1\",\n              \"new\": false,\n              \"why\": \"The nearly $50 billion of equity investments in frontier AI labs is the equity-investment side of the thesis, which compares disclosed guarantees/credit support with the equity investments NVIDIA has made; management's 'circular financing' concession and redeployment claim bear on the risk the thesis weighs.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev6\",\n          \"summary\": \"The 33 analyst estimates of NVIDIA's fiscal 2028 earnings per share range from $12.62 to $17.49 a share, a wide band for the year on which the forward multiple is priced, according to Trefis.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"The 33 estimates of fiscal 2028 earnings run from $12.62 to $17.49 a share, a wide band for the year the forward multiple is priced on.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"answer\": \"A37\",\n      \"article\": 7,\n      \"new_questions\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"new-1\",\n          \"question\": \"What total revenue will NVIDIA report for fiscal 2027 (the fiscal year ending late January 2027)?\",\n          \"outcome\": \"NVIDIA's reported total revenue for fiscal 2027 versus the prior year, as disclosed in its FY2027 annual results and Form 10-K; the item supports a Q2 FY2027 actual of $96.2 billion and Q3 FY2027 guidance of $108 billion (±2%, excluding China data-center compute revenue).\",\n          \"period\": \"Fiscal 2027 (year ending late January 2027); settled by NVIDIA's FY2027 annual results / Form 10-K, expected around February 2027 — the release of that fiscal year's results, per section 3 ([reason] quantity).\",\n          \"settled_by\": \"NVIDIA's fiscal 2027 annual results and Form 10-K (expected around February 2027), which report full-year total revenue.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"answer\": \"A38\",\n      \"article\": 5,\n      \"new_questions\": [],\n      \"kept_statements\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-1\",\n          \"summary\": \"As reported by qz.com (with market data attributed to Bloomberg), Nvidia's revenue and net income are each expected to grow by roughly 90% or more in its current fiscal year, even as the stock trades near its lowest valuation in more than a decade. The expectations are unattributed consensus figures rather than company guidance.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Nvidia $NVDA stock is trading near its lowest valuation in more than a decade, according to Bloomberg , even as the chipmaker's revenue and net income are each expected to grow by roughly 90% or more in its current fiscal year.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-2\",\n          \"summary\": \"Nvidia's gross margin came in at 75% in the prior quarter, but analyst estimates compiled by Bloomberg show it sliding under 72% by the fourth quarter, with a recovery expected thereafter. Rising costs for key components such as memory chips are cited as a central factor in the compression.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Nvidia 's gross margin came in at 75% last quarter but analyst estimates compiled by Bloomberg show it sliding under 72% by the fourth quarter, with a recovery expected thereafter. Rising costs for key components such as memory chips are a central factor.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-3\",\n          \"summary\": \"At its second-quarter earnings, Nvidia's revenue more than doubled year-over-year and the company projected 70% revenue growth in fiscal 2028, well above the 45% analysts had expected at the time. The stock rose roughly 7% after the report.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Nvidia stock climbed roughly 7% after its second-quarter earnings , when revenue more than doubled and the company projected 70% revenue growth in fiscal 2028 — well above the 45% analysts had expected at the time.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-4\",\n          \"summary\": \"David Russell, global head of market strategy at TradeStation, pointed to the growing threat of Nvidia customers building their own silicon, noting that Meta and Alphabet are among the major Nvidia buyers that have moved to design AI chips internally; he believes this shift will gradually erode Nvidia's pricing power and market share. The in-house chip programmes are described as already under way, with no dates or volumes given.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"David Russell, global head of market strategy at TradeStation, pointed to the growing threat of customers building their own silicon, noting that Meta $META Platforms and Alphabet $GOOGL are among the major Nvidia buyers that have moved to design AI chips internally — a shift he believes will gradually erode Nvidia 's pricing power and market share.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"answer\": \"A39\",\n      \"article\": 2,\n      \"new_questions\": [],\n      \"kept_statements\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-1\",\n          \"summary\": \"Zacks' consensus estimates project NVIDIA earnings of $2.47 per share for the current quarter (a +90% change from the year-ago quarter), $9.25 for the current fiscal year (+93.9% versus the prior year) and $15.33 for the next fiscal year (+65.8% versus what NVIDIA is expected to report a year ago). Over the last 30 days the Zacks Consensus Estimate changed +5.8% for the current quarter, +5.1% for the current fiscal year and +21.8% for the next fiscal year.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"For the current quarter, Nvidia is expected to post earnings of $2.47 per share, indicating a change of +90% from the year-ago quarter. The Zacks Consensus Estimate has changed +5.8% over the last 30 days.\",\n            \"For the current fiscal year, the consensus earnings estimate of $9.25 points to a change of +93.9% from the prior year. Over the last 30 days, this estimate has changed +5.1%.\",\n            \"For the next fiscal year, the consensus earnings estimate of $15.33 indicates a change of +65.8% from what Nvidia is expected to report a year ago. Over the past month, the estimate has changed +21.8%.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-2\",\n          \"summary\": \"Zacks reports consensus sales estimates for NVIDIA of $109.02 billion for the current quarter (a year-over-year change of +91.2%), $406.05 billion for the current fiscal year (+88%) and $671.95 billion for the next fiscal year (+65.5%).\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"For Nvidia, the consensus sales estimate for the current quarter of $109.02 billion indicates a year-over-year change of +91.2%. For the current and next fiscal years, $406.05 billion and $671.95 billion estimates indicate +88% and +65.5% changes, respectively.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"answer\": \"A40\",\n      \"article\": 4,\n      \"new_questions\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"answer\": \"A41\",\n      \"article\": 8,\n      \"new_questions\": [],\n      \"kept_statements\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e1\",\n          \"summary\": \"At the end of the second quarter of fiscal 2027, NVIDIA had committed $279 billion to secure supply and production capacity, up from $119 billion at the end of the first quarter; most commitments are tied to memory and manufacturing facilities needed for current and future data center products.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"At the end of the second quarter of fiscal 2027, the company had committed $279 billion to secure supply and production capacity, up from $119 billion in the first quarter. Most commitments are tied to memory and manufacturing facilities needed for current and future data center products.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"clean-2\",\n              \"new\": false,\n              \"why\": \"Reports the size of NVIDIA's supply and production capacity commitments ($279B at end-Q2 FY2027, up from $119B) — an interim data point directly on the purchase/supply commitment amount the thesis tracks at the next annual report.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e2\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA generated $96.22 billion in second-quarter fiscal 2027 revenues, up 106% year over year, while Data Center revenues surged 117% to $89.02 billion.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"N