eason] quantity).\",\n          \"settled_by\": \"NVIDIA's FY2028 fourth-quarter and full-year earnings release and FY2028 Form 10-K (around February 2028), which publish total revenue and its growth rate.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"new-2\",\n          \"question\": \"What gross margin will NVIDIA report for fiscal 2028?\",\n          \"outcome\": \"NVIDIA's reported fiscal 2028 gross margin versus the guided 72%–73% range, and whether memory cost inflation is offset by the price increases the company has already executed.\",\n          \"period\": \"Fiscal 2028 (year ending late January 2028); settled by NVIDIA's FY2028 fourth-quarter and full-year results and Form 10-K, expected around February 2028 — the release of that fiscal year's results, per section 3 ([reason] quantity).\",\n          \"settled_by\": \"NVIDIA's FY2028 fourth-quarter and full-year earnings release and FY2028 Form 10-K (around February 2028), which report the company's gross margin.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"kept_statements\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-1\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA management put the revenue opportunity from its Vera Rubin platform at about $40 billion per gigawatt of computing capacity, against about $25 billion per gigawatt with Blackwell, as reported by Trefis on 24 September 2026.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Management puts NVIDIA’s revenue opportunity at about $40 billion per gigawatt of capacity with Vera Rubin, against $25 billion with Blackwell.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-1\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"Management's estimate of revenue per gigawatt of installed Vera Rubin capacity (versus Blackwell) is a stated driver of the revenue the FY2028 guide depends on. It is an opportunity estimate, not a revenue forecast or a booked amount.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-2\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA's Vera Rubin production shipments began in August (2026), with purchase orders already received from every major hyperscaler, AI cloud and system OEM, as reported by Trefis on 24 September 2026.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Production shipments began in August, with purchase orders already in from every major hyperscaler, AI cloud, and system OEM.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"clean-4\",\n              \"new\": false,\n              \"why\": \"Reports that Vera Rubin production shipments began in August 2026 with purchase orders in hand — a step toward the volume customer shipments and first revenue recognition the thesis tracks; the item gives no shipment volume or revenue figure.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-1\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"Purchase orders from every major hyperscaler, AI cloud and system OEM are demand evidence behind the fiscal 2028 revenue guide; they are not recognised revenue.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-3\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA has guided to about 70% revenue growth for fiscal 2028, the first time it has given a full-year-ahead guide, according to Trefis's 24 September 2026 article.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"For fiscal 2028, management has guided about 70% revenue growth, the first time it has guided a full year ahead.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-1\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"Direct company guidance for the fiscal 2028 revenue growth the thesis tracks; the item notes the guide is the first full-year-ahead guide and is capped by supply, not demand.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-4\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA's CEO said demand is much greater than the 70% growth in the fiscal 2028 revenue guide and that supply is what holds the guide there; the CFO expects supply to stay a bottleneck at least through the end of fiscal 2028, per Trefis's 24 September 2026 article.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"The CEO says demand is much greater than 70%, and that supply is what holds the guide there. The CFO expects supply to stay a bottleneck at least through the end of fiscal 2028 and calls memory pricing extreme.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-1\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"Management frames the fiscal 2028 revenue guide as limited by supply rather than demand and expects the supply bottleneck to last at least through the end of fiscal 2028 — a constraint on delivering the guided revenue growth.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"question\": \"clean-2\",\n              \"new\": false,\n              \"why\": \"Inference: management calling supply the binding constraint through fiscal 2028 bears on how large NVIDIA's forward purchase and supply commitments may be; the item states no commitment amount.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-5\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA has invested nearly $50 billion in frontier AI labs, and management concedes some will call this circular financing while saying the compute can be redeployed to other customers, as reported by Trefis on 24 September 2026.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Some of that demand also leans on NVIDIA’s own balance sheet. NVIDIA has invested nearly $50 billion in frontier AI labs. Management concedes some will call this circular financing and says the compute can be redeployed to other customers.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"clean-1\",\n              \"new\": false,\n              \"why\": \"Quantifies the equity-investment side of NVIDIA's exposure to AI labs that the thesis compares with guaranteed credit support and revenue backstops; it states an investment amount, not any guarantee or backstop.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-6\",\n          \"summary\": \"The 33 analyst estimates for NVIDIA's fiscal 2028 earnings range from $12.62 to $17.49 a share, a band Trefis calls wide for the year the forward multiple is priced on, in its 24 September 2026 article.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"The 33 estimates of fiscal 2028 earnings run from $12.62 to $17.49 a share, a wide band for the year the forward multiple is priced on.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-7\",\n          \"summary\": \"Trefis said consensus has NVIDIA's earnings and revenue growing at a similar pace between fiscal 2027 and fiscal 2028, implying analysts assume profit margins hold roughly steady, and that for the forecast to hold the lost gross margin would have to be made up further down the income statement.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Consensus has earnings and revenue growing at a similar pace between fiscal 2027 and fiscal 2028, so analysts assume profit margins hold roughly steady.\",\n            \"For the forecast to hold, that lost gross margin has to be made up further down the income statement.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-2\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"States the consensus margin assumption (roughly steady profit margins) that sits against the lower guided gross margin, and that offsetting the gross-margin loss below the gross line is a condition for consensus forecasts — frames the gap the margin thesis tracks.\"\n            }\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"ev-8\",\n          \"summary\": \"NVIDIA guides its fiscal 2028 gross margin to settle in the 72% to 73% range, lower than before, because memory prices have risen more than management expected, helped by price increases NVIDIA has already executed, per Trefis's 24 September 2026 article.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Gross margin is guided lower. Memory prices have risen more than management expected, and the guide has that margin settling in the 72% to 73% range in fiscal 2028, helped by price increases NVIDIA has already executed.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": [\n            {\n              \"question\": \"new-2\",\n              \"new\": true,\n              \"why\": \"Direct company guidance for the fiscal 2028 gross margin the thesis tracks, with the stated causes (memory prices above management's expectations, partly offset by price increases already executed).\"\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"answer\": \"A44\",\n      \"article\": 3,\n      \"new_questions\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"answer\": \"A45\",\n      \"article\": 5,\n      \"new_questions\": [],\n      \"kept_statements\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e1\",\n          \"summary\": \"According to the qz.com article, Nvidia's revenue and net income are each expected to grow by roughly 90% or more in its current fiscal year, even as the stock trades near its lowest valuation in more than a decade. The expectation is reported without a named forecaster.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Nvidia $NVDA stock is trading near its lowest valuation in more than a decade, according to Bloomberg , even as the chipmaker's revenue and net income are each expected to grow by roughly 90% or more in its current fiscal year.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e2\",\n          \"summary\": \"Nvidia's gross margin came in at 75% in the quarter the article calls 'last quarter', the quarter preceding the 22 September 2026 publication.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Nvidia 's gross margin came in at 75% last quarter\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e3\",\n          \"summary\": \"Analyst estimates compiled by Bloomberg, cited by qz.com, show Nvidia's gross margin sliding under 72% by the fourth quarter, with a recovery expected thereafter; the article names rising costs for key components such as memory chips as a central factor.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Nvidia 's gross margin came in at 75% last quarter but analyst estimates compiled by Bloomberg show it sliding under 72% by the fourth quarter, with a recovery expected thereafter.\",\n            \"Rising costs for key components such as memory chips are a central factor.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e4\",\n          \"summary\": \"David Russell, global head of market strategy at TradeStation, said that Meta and Alphabet are among the major Nvidia buyers that have moved to design AI chips internally, a shift he believes will gradually erode Nvidia's pricing power and market share.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"David Russell, global head of market strategy at TradeStation, pointed to the growing threat of customers building their own silicon, noting that Meta $META Platforms and Alphabet $GOOGL are among the major Nvidia buyers that have moved to design AI chips internally — a shift he believes will gradually erode Nvidia 's pricing power and market share.\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"e5\",\n          \"summary\": \"Nvidia's revenue more than doubled in its second quarter, according to the article, which also notes the stock climbed roughly 7% after that earnings report.\",\n          \"passages\": [\n            \"Nvidia stock climbed roughly 7% after its second-quarter earnings , when revenue more than doubled\"\n          ],\n          \"linked_to\": []\n        },